# What is sent to the build of image/Containerfile. podman and buildah prefer
# <Containerfile>.containerignore over the .containerignore at the root of the
# build context, so this file replaces that one for the OS image.
#
# The image definition, and what the build stage compiles and installs
# (image/README.md, "Programs built into the image"): the sources of the TUR
# programs listed in image/programs.tsv, the shared crates, the application
# catalogue, and the licence that goes with the programs. A component that
# joins the image adds its directory here.
*
!image/
# TUR's artwork (the flat mark, the splash images, the wallpaper), installed
# by image/branding/branding.sh. The source logo and the drawing program are
# not needed in the build.
!branding/
branding/tur-logo.png
branding/render.py
# TUR's desktop theme and defaults (task D-04): the tree image/Containerfile
# copies, and nothing else of desktop/.
!desktop/data/rootfs/
!rust-toolchain.toml
!LICENSE.md
!NOTICE
!catalogue/
!crates/
!installer/tur-installer-core/
!services/tur-ai-local/
!services/tur-apps/
!services/tur-boot-health/
!services/tur-catalogue/
!services/tur-device-manager/
!services/tur-diagnostics/
!services/tur-pax/
!services/tur-pax-memory/
!services/tur-pax-providers/
!services/tur-runtime/
!services/tur-storage/
!services/tur-update/

# Never build output, whatever a working tree holds.
**/target/
